# Facts about Mir Ten (they/them).
# Formerly "Mira" (id `mira`); renamed 2026-10-15. See the note on `@npc mir` in cast.grim.

@fact mir.artificer
tier: surface
text: An artificer who smells of solder and ozone and has started at least one small fire.

@fact mir.owl
tier: personal
unlock: seen(mir_owl_gift) > 0
text: Built a clockwork owl that remembers deadlines, birthdays and, slightly, grudges.

@fact mir.notebooks
tier: personal
hint: Bring the hazelwood wand to Mir's Workshop.
unlock: rel(mir) >= 12
text: Three years of notebooks are the most precious things they own.

@fact mir.family
tier: personal
unlock: seen(mir_family_business) > 0
text: Their family runs a clockworks and thinks invention is a hobby. It is not a hobby.

@fact mir.name_day
tier: secret
unlock: seen(mir_name_day) > 0
text: Nobody ever remembered their name day before.

@fact mir.workshop
tier: personal
unlock: seen(mir_workshop_closed) > 0
text: After the third fire in a term, the faculty padlocked their workshop.

@fact mir.corridor
tier: personal
unlock: seen(mir_padlock) > 0
text: Locked out of a workshop, they will solder on the corridor floor for a week rather than stop. It's character-building, they say.

@fact mir.properly
tier: personal
hint: Spend a break in the capital, and call at the Ten Clockworks.
unlock: seen(clockworks_long_bench) > 0
text: At the family bench Mir works "properly": slow, silent and perfect, the way they never do at the castle. Their real workshop at home is a cupboard under the attic stairs.

@fact mir.drawer
tier: secret
hint: Call at the Ten Clockworks once you are good friends.
unlock: seen(clockworks_drawer) > 0
text: Their father keeps every invention Mir made as a child in a drawer marked "M.", labelled and oiled. He has never mentioned it to them.

@fact mir.sister
tier: personal
hint: Keep calling at the Ten Clockworks.
unlock: seen(clockworks_greta) > 0
text: Their older sister Greta will inherit the clockworks and is very good at it. She has never once been allowed to set anything on fire.
